<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>

<p>Kobo's arrival at Best Buy is the most concrete sign yet that the US e-reader market is no longer a one-brand aisle. Sixteen years of Kindle-only shelves gave Amazon a retail monopoly that no amount of online comparison could fully counter; a visible, returnable, discountable Kobo display changes the calculus for ordinary shoppers, not just enthusiasts.</p>

<p>Will it work? That depends on execution — demo units, trained staff, and consistent stock — the exact things that killed the Walmart partnership. But for EPUB readers, the direction is unmistakable: the open-format ecosystem is expanding in every channel, from software to firmware to retail. If you have been waiting for a low-risk way to buy into it, a Kobo from Best Buy is now the easiest option the US market has ever offered.</p>
